---
name: Appwrite Edge
description: The router behind Appwrite Sites. It maps every request to a deployment, serves previews, caches at the edge and scales runtimes per project.
---

Appwrite Sites needed something to sit in front of every customer domain and decide where a request goes. I built that router for the Sites launch in 2025. It now serves about 11 million requests a day.

Each request resolves a domain to a deployment and a region, then to a running runtime. Preview deployments, redirect rules, custom error pages and cache invalidation all live in the router. When a deployment changes, the region publishes an event and the edge drops its cached rule and runtime.

Runtimes run as Kubernetes pods. The edge scales them per project, keeps warm capacity on spare nodes, and reports every execution back to the region that owns it.
